	// RevokeAPIKeyWithBody Revoke an API token
	//
	// Withdraws a credential. It stops working on the very next request: the
	// resolution query filters on `revoked_at`, so there is no window.
	//
	// **The row is kept, not deleted.** "Was this token revoked, or was it always
	// broken?" is a support question and a deleted row answers it for nobody. A
	// revoked row holds a digest of a secret nobody has, so keeping it is not a
	// risk.
	//
	// A second revoke is a **409, not a 204**: an operator who clicked twice is
	// owed the truth, because a 204 the second time would leave them believing a
	// second live credential had just been destroyed.
