	// **The account comes from the path and the user from the session.** There is
	// no `account_id` or `user_id` in the body, and a body carrying either is a
	// 422. A credential is minted BY the caller FOR the caller's own account; there
	// is no subject field, and a machine credential that can be minted for somebody
	// else is a way for an owner to plant a credential somebody did not choose to
	// hold.
	//
	// **`token` is returned here and nowhere else, ever.** It is shown once, at
	// creation, and there is no endpoint that re-reads it — not because one is
	// missing but because there is nothing left to print: the row holds a SHA-256
	// of a 256-bit value. A caller that loses it mints another. It is never in a
	// cookie, because a credential in a cookie is one a browser silently attaches
	// to a request its holder did not intend, which is what core means by "no
	// cookies for API traffic".
