	// RegisterOIDCClientWithBodyWithResponse Register an OpenID Connect client
	//
	// Registers a relying party: the credential a product presents at the token
	// endpoint when it runs an authorization-code flow against this service.
	//
	// **Owner only.** Adding a client is adding a new way for code to arrive in
	// this product and get a token back out, so a member of the account is 403
	// and a non-member is 404.
