// StartMFAEnrollmentWithBodyWithResponse Generate a TOTP secret
//
// Generates a secret with `crypto/rand`, stores it **unconfirmed**, and returns
// it once with its `otpauth://` provisioning URI.
//
// `secret` and `provisioning_uri` are returned here and **never again**: there
// is no endpoint that re-reads them, so a client that loses this response
// starts a new enrollment, which mints a new secret. The reasoning is the one
// an OIDC `client_secret` follows: a secret this service can produce again is a
// secret this service is storing, and a stored TOTP secret is a second factor
// for whoever reads the database.
//
// **A pending enrollment is not MFA.** It expires in ten minutes, the login
// path reads only confirmed rows, and no session is issued until
// `/confirm`. A stored-but-never-confirmed secret is exactly the state that
// locks somebody out of their own account.
//
// On an account that **already** has a credential this starts a **rotation**,
// and `code` is then required. The existing secret stays live until the
// replacement is confirmed, so an abandoned rotation costs nothing; on
// confirmation the old credential is deleted, which is how its codes stop being
// accepted.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /v1/mfa/enrollments (the `StartMFAEnrollment` operationId).
