// CompleteSecondFactorWithBodyWithResponse Answer a second factor and start the session
//
// The second half of a login for an account with a second factor, and **the
// only route in this service that turns a second factor into a session**.
//
// The session is created inside the same transaction that consumes the
// challenge, so a challenge cannot be answered twice and a code cannot buy two
// sessions.
//
// **The challenge is accepted in the cookie or in the body**, and both are
// supported on purpose: cafaye's conventions say "no cookies for API traffic",
// and `POST /v1/session` returns the session token in the body as well as in
// the cookie precisely so a non-browser client has a way in. The explicit body
// value wins when both are present, for the reason `GET /v1/me` prefers the
// `Authorization` header over the cookie.
//
// A code is accepted within **one step either side** of the current one, so a
// TOTP code is live for 90 seconds rather than 30. Zero skew would refuse any
// code typed near a step boundary, which is when a user is most likely to be
// reading digits off a screen, and a second factor with a visible failure rate
// gets turned off rather than retried. Two steps or more would be ninety more
// seconds during which a phished code still works.
//
// **A code cannot be accepted twice.** Replay is the standard attack against
// TOTP, and this service records the exact steps consumed: a code already used
// is refused for the whole window, and refusing it costs nothing to the user
// beyond the next 30-second period.
//
// Five consecutive wrong codes lock the second factor for fifteen minutes, and
// that counter is **separate from the password's**.
//
// Takes any type of body and a specified content type, and returns a wrapper object for the known response body format(s).
//
// Corresponds with POST /v1/session/mfa (the `CompleteSecondFactor` operationId).
func (c *ClientWithResponses) CompleteSecondFactorWithBodyWithResponse(ctx context.Context, contentType string, body io.Reader, reqEditors ...RequestEditorFn) (*CompleteSecondFactorResponse, error) {
	rsp, err := c.CompleteSecondFactorWithBody(ctx, contentType, body, reqEditors...)
	if err != nil {
		return nil, err
	}
	return ParseCompleteSecondFactorResponse(rsp)
}

